'''Artés''' ([[Baliscano language|Baliscano]] meaning "small fortified hill") is an island that sits in [[Salto Bay]] within the borders of the [[Castejón|Castejón Metropolis]]. It is one of the [[Salto Islands]], and is undergoing expansion through {{W|land reclamation}} as part of the [[Nueva Castejón]] project. The [[Artés Tunnel]] runs through its center and connects the western and eastern spans of the [[Salto Bay Bridge]], linking [[Ampurias]] with [[Trinacria]].

Following the construction of the {{W|sugar factory}} and it's {{W|company town}} in 1877, the island's population quickly grew. The sugar factory was severely damaged by revolting workers during the [[Cantonal War]]. The factory was eventually rebuilt and converted into the [[Muséu de los Trabajadores del Azúcar|Museum of the Sugarworkers]].

According to the [[2025 Baliscan census]], Artés has a land area of {{convert|8.19|km2}} with a total population of 38,047.

